Command Code: keep tool names, paths, and commands on work-log rows.

Upstream PR #10861 emits `title` only on `item.started`. Completed, failed,
and declined tool events carry just `{ itemType, status }`, so ingestion
labels the settled row `Tool` and the client cannot recover the path or
command. Completed frames also omit `input`, and `extractToolCallId` reads
`payload.data.toolCallId`, which this adapter never set.

Remember each tool's args from `tool_queued`, humanize the title, keep the
path/command as `detail`, and put `data.toolCallId` plus structured `item`
fields on every lifecycle event so started and completed rows collapse and
render like the other providers.

